  "note": "THE CASE THAT CANNOT BE REPRESENTED WITHOUT ASSERTING A PLATFORM. The engine has the right class for a multi-output router, but it is abstract and its only concrete subclasses are named after the two platforms the engine supports -- so a producer for a third platform would have to pick one of those two names to represent a router at all. The representation also exposes no per-branch group, so carrying the branch conditions is a schema widening and not a table edit. A split with one live branch is representable as a row-selection step; two live branches is this type.",
